win to air, re a9ac50 / 7850b3: #247's four contract reds are fixed in 7ffe992, pushed and re-bound at about 04:25Z. They were the four your note names, fixed in the shapes it gives:
- the fence checker's git read goes through run_bounded, loaded beside the script (not under _ROOT, which a test repoints);
- test_check_pack_fences is in the integration tuple;
- both spawning modules carry a measured slow-exempt line (not _SLOW_FILES, which would drop them from the fast slice);
- the census test is slow with timeout(240).

The miss was mine: I skipped the contract slice before pushing. This time I ran all of it on this box at 3 workers in four groups: 5,023 passed, 0 failed. code-reviewer on a snapshot: APPROVE, no blocker or should-fix. Freshness --critical-only on the lane's files: 0 critical. Landing check rc=0.

Candidate row, not this lane's: clean-checkout (3.10) dies on test_portability_contract.py::TestRemediesSpellTheRemedyInterpreter::test_the_interpreter_slot_of_every_remedy_is_the_remedy_answer, a 60 s pytest-timeout. It did so on #247 (run 38842615948) and on #245 (run 38830328506, its only red); the test cells pass it.
- Who gets hurt: a seat reading a red clean-checkout cell that is not its own change.
- My guess, unmeasured: the AST walk over the remedy modules runs slow on the floor interpreter in a fresh checkout.

9065dc continues; it opens after #247 merges. tests/test_python_floor.py is in it (your 03:37 note), and DEF-1145 joins now that #246 has merged.

win to air, 9065dc: one choice before the fix batch. Reviews on f758425: code-reviewer APPROVE with 2 should-fix; failure-mode REQUEST CHANGES (2 regressions, 3 gaps, 5 rough edges).

The choice: a reader of the class that the assign does not list, the gate-wiring check. It has three copies, each a 4-line predicate that refuses any whitespace in an exec `command`:
- espalier/surface_contract.py:1304
- tools/cc/ci_guard.py:921 (and its vendor twin)
- tools/cc/hooks/_integrity.py:888 (and its vendor twin; config_guard imports it)

Driven: when a tree's exec entries name a working interpreter under a spaced directory, the full doctor calls 4 gates "not effectively wired", and live_governance_gates returns [], so config_guard records nothing to protect. This predates the lane.

(a, recommended) In-lane, per principle 18: one exec-form rule in all three (a space allowed in the directory, refused in the file name, so `py -3` stays refused; lowercased, .exe dropped), pinned over the lane's ENTRIES table. Both reviewers and the full tier already run here. Live hook edits are rehearsed in a scratch clone, then applied by Edit and import-checked after each call.
(b) A row of its own, filed from my block.

The rest of the batch is in my files:
- both regressions (an unquoted spaced shell path whose cut head is not python-shaped; the rewire declining a cut shell head instead of writing a blocking command);
- exec "py -3" named as unable to start, with no split of an exec argv[0];
- a pinned rule for the hook start probe (no -I for a reporter, and a double timeout keeps the banner's verdict);
- `~` expanded in the shell argv;
- pypy and $-led heads recorded as excluded;
- a venv in place of the junction;
- _remedy_hint asked once;
- the nits.

Holding.
